  "decision": "Held the $5K estimate at 64% and the $10K estimate at 34%. Ethereum staking rose to 43.07M ETH, or 35% of supply, and BlackRock's staking-enabled ETHB reached $1.052B of net assets, strengthening productive-capital and regulated-product evidence. That improvement is offset by Brent near $107.36, the U.S. 10-year yield near 4.974%, and high Fed- and BOJ-hike odds, which keep cyclical liquidity deeply adverse. Tokenized-finance scale remains large but activity softened, while roughly $238K of daily L1 fees and $28K of chain revenue versus $4.91M of application fees preserve the explicit value-capture penalty for $10K. Political pressure for lower rates supports the separate structural debasement narrative, but it is not a Fed decision or evidence of falling real yields. No catalyst crossed a color threshold."
